Main test (Spec A+B, both samples, 20 cells): 1 excess-return cells clear a 90% CI; tiers (40 cells): 5; time of day (30 cells): 2. Total hypotheses 352 incl. 2 backtests; at a 90 pct CI expect about 35 false positives by chance.
Strongest cell: T4_tod spec B all above session 1mo, n=331, excess +76 bp, 90% CI [+24, +131], t-like 2.36.
Strategy on it (long at close of print day, hold 21d, 1bp per side): 44 trades, Sharpe 0.67, max DD -28.7 pct, total return +53.0 pct, in market 924/1202 days. SPY buy and hold over the same window: Sharpe 0.74, max DD -24.5 pct.
Long/short toward the block side (long after above prints, short after below, hold 21d, one per day, 1bp per side): 54 trades, Sharpe -0.02, max DD -34.6 pct, total return -8.0 pct.
Verdict: FAIL. Spec A 'below' cells (-120 bp at 1d) are the print-day move leaking into the window, not a signal. In Spec B the only recurring pattern is 1mo drift toward the print side (above +57 to +100 bp, below -33 to -60 bp, t-like at most 2.4), it is one effect seen in nested cells, it does not survive a 352-hypothesis haircut, gap-fill hit rates are within 11 points of the matched baseline, and neither tradeable version beats SPY buy and hold over the same window.
Caveat: 4.8 years of SPY, mostly a bull market, with ~3 prints per event day; one-event-per-day n is the honest n.
